message.content:
{
  "summary": "This bill proposes the Menstrual Hygiene Products Accessibility Act. It would require local education agencies and public charter schools to provide feminine hygiene products, such as tampons, panty liners, menstrual cups, and sanitary napkins, at no charge for student use. These products must be available in all women's and girls' bathrooms, all locker rooms, and with the school nurse in eligible school buildings, which are defined as senior high schools. Bathrooms and locker rooms designated for staff or teacher use are excluded from this requirement. The department of education may provide guidance and policies to help schools comply. The act would take effect July 1, 2025."
}
